clearly. - **White plays Kxb2:** Black plays axb1=Q+ Kxb1. White's queening
threat is gone, and Black is still a full minor piece up with bishop and knight
against a knight. - **White plays Rxc1:** Black plays bxc1=Q+ Kxc1 a1=Q+ and
wins as well. - **White plays Nb3:** Black takes it with Nxb3 and can then
promote. } 47. Rxb2 a1=Q { [%emt 0:00:17] [%think 1046] [%out 1194] [%in 2]
